@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "koroneiki"

Feature: Koroneiki Product API Permissioning
	Testing Koroneiki Product API Permissioning functionality.

Teardown:
	* I tear down the external links for the product "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" on koroneiki with the following entity id values
	| 1234 |
	* I tear down the products on koroneiki with the following names
	| Liferay Digital Experience Platform |
	| Liferay Portal                      |

Scenario: Create product attempt by non permissioned user
	Koroneiki products that are attempted to be created via API by non permissioned users should not be created.

	Given I attempt to create a product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" as a non permissioned user
	Then I should not be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform"

Scenario: View product attempt by non permissioned user
	Koroneiki products should not be viewable for non permissioned users.

	Given I create a product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform"
	Then I should not be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" as a non permissioned user

Scenario: Update product attempt by non permissioned user
	Koroneiki products that are attempted to be updated via API by non permissioned users should not be updated.

	Given I create a product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform"
	And I attempt to update a product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" to have the new name "Liferay Portal" as a non permissioned user
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform"
	And I should not be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "Liferay Portal"
	And I should not be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" as a non permissioned user

Scenario: Remove product attempt by non permissioned user
	Koroneiki products removed via API should not be viewable via API by non permissioned users.

	Given I create a product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform"
	And I attempt to delete a koroneiki product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" as a non permissioned user
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform"
	And I should not be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" as a non permissioned user

Scenario: Create product external link attempt by non permissioned user
	Koroneiki product external links should not be able to be created via API by non permissioned users.

	Given I create a product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform"
	And I attempt to create an external link on a product "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" with the following values as a non permissioned user
	| Domain      | liferaydxp |
	| Entity Id   | 1234       |
	| Entity Name | LiferayDXP |
	Then the external link with the entity id "1234" should not be present on the product "Liferay Digital Experience Platform"

Scenario: View product external link attempt by non permissioned user
	Koroneiki product external links should not be viewable by non permissioned users.

	Given I create a product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform"
	And I create an external link on a product "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" with the following values
	| Domain      | liferaydxp |
	| Entity Id   | 1234       |
	| Entity Name | LiferayDXP |
	Then the external link with the entity id "1234" should be present on the product "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" with the following values
	| Domain      | liferaydxp |
	| Entity Id   | 1234       |
	| Entity Name | LiferayDXP |
	And the external link with the entity id "1234" on the product "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" should not be visible to a non permissioned user
	And I should not be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" using the external link domain "liferaydxp" and entity name "LiferayDXP" and entity id "1234" as a non permissioned user

Scenario: Remove product external link attempt by non permissioned user
	Koroneiki product external links should not be removable by non permissioned users.

	Given I create a product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform"
	And I create an external link on a product "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" with the following values
	| Domain      | liferaydxp |
	| Entity Id   | 1234       |
	| Entity Name | LiferayDXP |
	And I attempt to delete an external link with the entity id "1234" on the product "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" as a non permissioned user
	Then the external link with the entity id "1234" should be present on the product "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" with the following values
	| Domain      | liferaydxp |
	| Entity Id   | 1234       |
	| Entity Name | LiferayDXP |
	And the external link with the entity id "1234" on the product "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" should not be visible to a non permissioned user
	And I should not be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" using the external link domain "liferaydxp" and entity name "LiferayDXP" and entity id "1234" as a non permissioned user